.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \(dqserver.h\(dq

void observe_cleanup(void);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tears down the observability subsystem for the current session.
If pre/post command hooks are registered, they are unregistered via
\f[CR]unregister_pre_command_hook()\f[R] and
\f[CR]unregister_post_command_hook()\f[R].
The observe file descriptor is reset to \-1 and the level is set to 0.
.PP
This function is called during session teardown to ensure no stale hook
callbacks remain.
It is safe to call even if \f[CR]observe_init()\f[R] was never called or
if hooks were never registered.
.SH PARAMETERS
None.
.SH RETURN VALUE
None.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]observe_init\f[R](3), \f[CR]observe_set_level\f[R](3)
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Does \f[B]not\f[R] close the observe fd; the session handler owns that
resource.
.IP \(bu 2
After cleanup, the observe module will silently discard any hook
invocations that may still be in flight (the \f[CR]observe_fd < 0\f[R]
guard in the hook callbacks handles this).
